    "https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/karriereportal.details?asg_id_in=15893": {
      "title": "University Assistant (PhD position)",
      "description": "University Assistant (PhD position) Back PDF output Apply online University Assistant (PhD position) Start date/duration: from 15.09.2026 for 4 years Administrative unit: Department of Company and Taxation Law Extent of employment: 20 hours per week; will be increased to 30 hours per week once the dissertation agreement has been signed Job Description: Your responsibilities: in Austrian, international or European tax law A PhD thesis in the field of Austrian, international or European tax law Independent research and participation in tax law research projects: either independently or in collaboration with the professor, you will author publications in specialist journals (in German and, where applicable, English) and contribute to commentaries on legislation Teaching and involvement in innovative courses: You will teach tax law independently and assist in delivering courses Participation in professional development courses and the opportunity to attend conferences in Austria and abroad: You will become part of the Austrian and international tax law community Opportunity for research stays abroad Organisational and administrative tasks: You will assist in organising specialist conferences and support the acquisition of research projects Your profile: A completed degree in law or commercial law (Masterâ€™s, Magister or Diplom degree) Above-average knowledge of the Austrian tax law system Excellent verbal and written communication skills Curiosity and a passion for academic work Very good command of German and, ideally, very good command of English (spoken and written) Ability to work within a dynamic team Enthusiasm, resilience and attention to detail Relevant practical experience in tax law would be an advantage Please include a written outline of your proposed doctoral thesis (max. 5 pages) with your application Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/REWI-15893 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#dissertationsstellen Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agreement) for 20 hours per week amounts to € 1.888 per month (14 times)*. The salary will be increased to € 2.832 for 30 hours per week once the dissertation agreement has been signed and sent to the Personnel Department. The salary will be higher if you have worked in a similar position before. * as of 2026 Application: We are looking forward to receiving your online application by 20.11.2026 stating the code REWI-15893 NAV_KP246 Contact: If you have any questions about the tender, please contact: Matthias Baumgartner Phone: +512 507 83211 Email: matthias.baumgartner@uibk.ac.at The University of Innsbruck emphasizes equal opportunities and diversity in its personnel policy. The University of Innsbruck strives to increase the percentage of women and thus expressly encourages women to apply. This is particularely true for leading positions and scientific job offers. In case of underrepresentation women with the same qualifications will be given priority. The University of Innsbruck bears the \"We are inclusive\" seal of approval. We therefore expressly invite qualified individuals with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses to apply. Back PDF output Apply online teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail"
    }
  },
